      "supports_or_contradicts": "supports",
      "independence_group": "gesetze-im-internet.de:law_20a",
      "copy_risk": "low",
      "evidence_summary": "Section 20a of the Residence Act defines the Opportunity Card as a residence permit to look for work, sets eligibility as either skilled-worker status or enough points, requires secured livelihood, lists the qualification and language conditions for the points path, limits permitted work, and sets validity of up to one year with a possible follow-on card.",
